-- and the invariance theorem for the oriented molecule: an observation of an atom invariant under
-- the automorphisms that preserve handedness is constant on the oriented orbits. This is the
-- statement a predicted spectrum needs, and it is strictly weaker in its hypothesis than the graph
-- version, because the group is smaller.
or-orbit-invariant : (S : Oriented) → (B : Type 0) → (f : mol-atoms (or-mol S) → B) → ((a : OrAuto S) → (x : mol-atoms (or-mol S)) → f (auto-fun (or-mol S) (fst a) x) ≡ f x) → (x : mol-atoms (or-mol S)) → (y : mol-atoms (or-mol S)) → OrOrbit S x y → f x ≡ f y
or-orbit-invariant S B f h x y o = concat (sym (h (fst o) x)) (cong f (snd o))
